68mK3sTAnz2upTy4RF8pii9Sz\nYVn6bBi8j65bxgk3OXDgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-21T16:01:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126489721?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sujeet-pro","id":126489721,"login":"sujeet-pro","node_id":"U_kgDOB4oUeQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/commit/443538ca8d4ac25c3ea70f3854d99850780ee907","node_id":"C_kwDOSIxvO9oAKDQ0MzUzOGNhOGQ0YWMyNWMzZWE3MGYzODU0ZDk5ODUwNzgwZWU5MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/commit/86f16eccc3af6755af3504e1e5847b135894b385","sha":"86f16eccc3af6755af3504e1e5847b135894b385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/commits/86f16eccc3af6755af3504e1e5847b135894b385"}],"sha":"443538ca8d4ac25c3ea70f3854d99850780ee907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/commits/443538ca8d4ac25c3ea70f3854d99850780ee907"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126489721?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sujeet-pro","id":126489721,"login":"sujeet-pro","node_id":"U_kgDOB4oUeQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/commits/86f16eccc3af6755af3504e1e5847b135894b385/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-20T06:03:25Z","email":"126489721+sujeet-pro@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sujeet Jaiswal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-20T06:03:25Z","email":"126489721+sujeet-pro@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sujeet Jaiswal"},"message":"chore(ai-docs): refresh skills + validators for diagramkit 0.3 + pagesmith 0.9.8\n\nThe Pagesmith and diagramkit packages moved their agent-facing guidance under\n`node_modules/<pkg>/skills/<skill>/references/` (Pagesmith) and added a full\nper-engine skill set (diagramkit). This change refreshes the repo''s\nAI-facing surface to match.\n\nSkills + AI docs\n- Replace flat `sp-*` skill files with folder-shaped `.agents/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md`\n  bodies (`prj-doc`, `prj-article`, `prj-blog`, `prj-content`, `prj-diagrams`,\n  `prj-validate`, `prj-sync`). Each prj-* skill cross-loads the version-pinned\n  upstream `pagesmith-core-*`, `pagesmith-site-*`, and `diagramkit-*` skills.\n- `.claude/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` are now\n  thin pointers (frontmatter + a one-line follow-link) to the canonical\n  `.agents/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` body.\n- Repoint every `node_modules/@pagesmith/<pkg>/ai-guidelines/...` reference in\n  `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `ai-guidelines/`, and `.cursor/rules/` to the new\n  `node_modules/@pagesmith/<pkg>/skills/<skill>/references/...` paths.\n- Fix `.cursor/rules/content.mdc`''s diagram embed example (was raw HTML\n  `<figure><img>` — replaced with the markdown-image themed-pair pattern that\n  the site validator actually enforces).\n\nValidation scripts\n- `package.json`: route `validate:content`, `validate:build`, and\n  `validate:full` through `scripts/validate-pagesmith.ts` (which already\n  composes `@pagesmith/site`''s `validateContent`, `validateBuildOutput`,\n  `loadContentSchemaMap`, and `formatContentValidationReport`). Add\n  `validate:diagrams[:json]`, `validate:all`, and `diagrams:doctor`.\n- Replace the dead `scripts/validate-build.ts` reference with the\n  `validate-pagesmith.ts --build` mode.\n- New `scripts/validate-diagrams.ts`: scopes the `diagramkit validate` audit\n  to `**/diagrams/` folders so legacy hand-authored `.inline.svg` files in\n  `assets/` don''t produce false-positive `CONTAINS_FOREIGN_OBJECT` /\n  `EXTERNAL_RESOURCE` warnings unrelated to the diagramkit pipeline.\n\nDiagram cleanup (every Mermaid source + every rendered SVG)\n- New `scripts/fix-mermaid-html-labels.ts` (one-shot): adds the\n  `%%{init: {''htmlLabels'': false}}%%` directive to every `.mermaid` source so\n  Mermaid emits SVG-native labels instead of `<foreignObject>` HTML labels.\n  This was applied to all 609 sources and removed all\n  `CONTAINS_FOREIGN_OBJECT` warnings from rendered diagram SVGs.\n- Re-render every diagram (`npm run diagrams:force`) so the regenerated\n  outputs match the new sources.\n- Delete 1170 orphan `.dark.svg` / `.light.svg` files (legacy diagramkit\n  naming) and update the two blog files that still referenced them\n  (`content/blogs/chrome-developer-setup/README.md`,\n  `content/blogs/editor-terminal-setup/README.md`) to the current\n  `-dark.svg` / `-light.svg` form.\n\nBug fixes\n- `scripts/check-orphans.ts`: previously reported every image with a markdown\n  caption (`![alt](src \"caption\")`) as orphan because the regex captured\n  `src \"caption\"` as the path. Strip optional title and query/hash fragments\n  so legitimate references are recognised. (The original bug would have\n  caused 14 production assets to be deleted as \"orphans\"; the build then fails\n  because the markdown still references them.)\n- `playwright.config.ts`: `withBasePath(bp, \"/\")` returns the base path\n  without a trailing slash, but `vite preview` only serves the index at the\n  trailing-slash form. Append the trailing slash explicitly so the playwright\n  webServer health check stops timing out.\n- `tests/e2e/navigation.spec.ts`: fix three pre-existing test bugs that\n  surfaced once the playwright webServer started succeeding —\n  (a) tolerate both `/articles/#` and `/articles#` series-card hrefs\n  (the site uses `trailingSlash: false`),\n  (b) target the section breadcrumb specifically (the locator matched two\n  links to `/articles` because series articles render two breadcrumb crumbs\n  pointing at the section),\n  (c) use Playwright''s `toHaveTitle()` instead of `toContainText(\"title\")`,\n  which doesn''t read text inside `<head>`.\n\nAll checks pass:\n  - 0 type errors (tsc), 0 lint errors (oxlint), 0 fmt issues (oxfmt)\n  - unit tests: 13/13 pass\n  - e2e tests: 204/204 pass (desktop-chrome + tablet + mobile)\n  - npm run validate, validate:full, validate:dist, validate:orphans: 0/0\n  - npm run validate:diagrams: 1218/1218 valid, 0 invalid\n    (59 LOW_CONTRAST_TEXT warnings remain on legacy diagrams using mermaid''s\n    default light pastel palette — needs bespoke per-diagram visual review;\n    not introduced by this change.)\n\nMade-with: Cursor","tree":{"sha":"7c4bd3a9e87f33c4ef5dafb418a1e7e7b8e6582f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/git/trees/7c4bd3a9e87f33c4ef5dafb418a1e7e7b8e6582f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sujeet-pro/sujeet.pro/git/commits/86f16eccc3af6755af3504e1e5847b135894b385","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c4bd3a9e87f33c4ef5dafb418a1e7e7b8e6582f\nparent 854c33e67cf44d5f577c38a227ef1dc857fd8bf7\nauthor Sujeet Jaiswal <126489721+sujeet-pro@users.noreply.github.com> 1776665005 +0530\ncommitter Sujeet Jaiswal <126489721+sujeet-pro@users.noreply.github.com> 1776665005 +0530\n\nchore(ai-docs): refresh skills + validators for diagramkit 0.3 + pagesmith 0.9.8\n\nThe Pagesmith and diagramkit packages moved their agent-facing guidance under\n`node_modules/<pkg>/skills/<skill>/references/` (Pagesmith) and added a full\nper-engine skill set (diagramkit). This change refreshes the repo''s\nAI-facing surface to match.\n\nSkills + AI docs\n- Replace flat `sp-*` skill files with folder-shaped `.agents/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md`\n  bodies (`prj-doc`, `prj-article`, `prj-blog`, `prj-content`, `prj-diagrams`,\n  `prj-validate`, `prj-sync`). Each prj-* skill cross-loads the version-pinned\n  upstream `pagesmith-core-*`, `pagesmith-site-*`, and `diagramkit-*` skills.\n- `.claude/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` are now\n  thin pointers (frontmatter + a one-line follow-link) to the canonical\n  `.agents/skills/prj-*/SKILL.md` body.\n- Repoint every `node_modules/@pagesmith/<pkg>/ai-guidelines/...` reference in\n  `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `ai-guidelines/`, and `.cursor/rules/` to the new\n  `node_modules/@pagesmith/<pkg>/skills/<skill>/references/...` paths.\n- Fix `.cursor/rules/content.mdc`''s diagram embed example (was raw HTML\n  `<figure><img>` — replaced with the markdown-image themed-pair pattern that\n  the site validator actually enforces).\n\nValidation scripts\n- `package.json`: route `validate:content`, `validate:build`, and\n  `validate:full` through `scripts/validate-pagesmith.ts` (which already\n  composes `@pagesmith/site`''s `validateContent`, `validateBuildOutput`,\n  `loadContentSchemaMap`, and `formatContentValidationReport`). Add\n  `validate:diagrams[:json]`, `validate:all`, and `diagrams:doctor`.\n- Replace the dead `scripts/validate-build.ts` reference with the\n  `validate-pagesmith.ts --build` mode.\n- New `scripts/validate-diagrams.ts`: scopes the `diagramkit validate` audit\n  to `**/diagrams/` folders so legacy hand-authored `.inline.svg` files in\n  `assets/` don''t produce false-positive `CONTAINS_FOREIGN_OBJECT` /\n  `EXTERNAL_RESOURCE` warnings unrelated to the diagramkit pipeline.\n\nDiagram cleanup (every Mermaid source + every rendered SVG)\n- New `scripts/fix-mermaid-html-labels.ts` (one-shot): adds the\n  `%%{init: {''htmlLabels'': false}}%%` directive to every `.mermaid` source so\n  Mermaid emits SVG-native labels instead of `<foreignObject>` HTML labels.\n  This was applied to all 609 sources and removed all\n  `CONTAINS_FOREIGN_OBJECT` warnings from rendered diagram SVGs.\n- Re-render every diagram (`npm run diagrams:force`) so the regenerated\n  outputs match the new sources.\n- Delete 1170 orphan `.dark.svg` / `.light.svg` files (legacy diagramkit\n  naming) and update the two blog files that still referenced them\n  (`content/blogs/chrome-developer-setup/README.md`,\n  `content/blogs/editor-terminal-setup/README.md`) to the current\n  `-dark.svg` / `-light.svg` form.\n\nBug fixes\n- `scripts/check-orphans.ts`: previously reported every image with a markdown\n  caption (`![alt](src \"caption\")`) as orphan because the regex captured\n  `src \"caption\"` as the path. Strip optional title and query/hash fragments\n  so legitimate references are recognised. (The original bug would have\n  caused 14 production assets to be deleted as \"orphans\"; the build then fails\n  because the markdown still references them.)\n- `playwright.config.ts`: `withBasePath(bp, \"/\")` returns the base path\n  without a trailing slash, but `vite preview` only serves the index at the\n  trailing-slash form. Append the trailing slash explicitly so the playwright\n  webServer health check stops timing out.\n- `tests/e2e/navigation.spec.ts`: fix three pre-existing test bugs that\n  surfaced once the playwright webServer started succeeding —\n  (a) tolerate both `/articles/#` and `/articles#` series-card hrefs\n  (the site uses `trailingSlash: false`),\n  (b) target the section breadcrumb specifically (the locator matched two\n  links to `/articles` because series articles render two breadcrumb crumbs\n  pointing at the section),\n  (c) use Playwright''s `toHaveTitle()` instead of `toContainText(\"title\")`,\n  which doesn''t read text inside `<head>`.\n\nAll checks pass:\n  - 0 type errors (tsc), 0 lint errors (oxlint), 0 fmt issues (oxfmt)\n  - unit tests: 13/13 pass\n  - e2e tests: 204/204 pass (desktop-chrome + tablet + mobile)\n  - npm run validate, validate:full, validate:dist, validate:orphans: 0/0\n  - npm run validate:diagrams: 1218/1218 valid, 0 invalid\n    (59 LOW_CONTRAST_TEXT warnings remain on legacy diagrams using mermaid''s\n    default light pastel palette — needs bespoke per-diagram visual review;\n    not introduced by this change.)\n\nMade-with: Cursor\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgi6zpiTH+gOIYvKjmL9bpRxVFyU\nPpWOq5+lnV0Qkf39wAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIPivb5w6ir3+cV78gZI9FIcLoHZJkzzxh4RnLZuVwgOergIY56Rxz6JOQLSoP9seD\nSsfKvICwQ3HXv3exfbBgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-21T16:01:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126489721?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sujeet-pro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sujeet-pro","id":126489721,"login":"sujeet-pro","node_id":"U_kgDOB4oUeQ","organizations_url":"https://ap