zE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tona3922","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tona3922/microfrontend-test-app/commits/26d79dd03e875febb03f116bdf828b475bee81b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T17:24:24Z","email":"vothaitoan12@gmail.com","name":"tona3922"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T17:24:24Z","email":"vothaitoan12@gmail.com","name":"tona3922"},"message":"Add OAuth2 (Google + GitHub) with PKCE to auth MFE and shell\n\nshell:\n- oauth.ts: PKCE utilities (verifier, challenge, state), provider\n  configs for Google and GitHub, token exchange, user-info fetch\n- AuthContext: adds initiateOAuth() (PKCE redirect) and\n  handleOAuthCallback() (state verification + token exchange)\n- App: OAuthCallbackHandler detects ?code= on mount, calls\n  handleOAuthCallback, cleans URL via history.replaceState\n- .env.example: documents VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,\n  VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID, VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN_PROXY_URL\n\nreact-app (AuthWidget MFE):\n- Adds \"Continue with Google\" and \"Continue with GitHub\" buttons\n- Calls onOAuthLogin(provider) prop — shell owns the redirect\n- Standalone main.tsx shows an alert explaining OAuth needs the shell\n\nNote: Google token exchange works from the browser via PKCE.\nGitHub requires a backend proxy (no CORS on their token endpoint);\npoint VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN_PROXY_URL at your own server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"152919f679aed0c9aaeefb75e46d9cdc0c85319e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tona3922/microfrontend-test-app/git/trees/152919f6