yNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/1dc9b80352b954210db9da05c3f6f819afc3ce82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T22:56:53Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T22:56:53Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"docs: trim README + architecture; fix React version drift\n\n- README: 482 → 347 lines. Push learning-objective detail to\n  docs/learning_objectives.md, condense retrospective, drop\n  per-decision \"when this would change\" boilerplate.\n- docs/architecture.md: 271 → 198 lines. Tighten /authorize +\n  /token walkthroughs, condense worker pseudocode, fix React\n  18 → 19 (web/package.json is React 19).\n- learning_objectives.md, rfcs.md: small voice fixes (third-\n  person → first person).\n\nAudited all route/endpoint/CLI/migration/Makefile claims\nagainst the code; no other drift found.","tree":{"sha":"0e019106dfcaaaaa1a5f38a0e63b5f19c535b5d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/0e019106dfcaaaaa1a5f38a0e63b5f19c535b5d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/1dc9b80352b954210db9da05c3f6f819afc3ce82","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/1dc9b80352b954210db9da05c3f6f819afc3ce82","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDFkYzliODAzNTJiOTU0MjEwZGI5ZGEwNWMzZjZmODE5YWZjM2NlODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63","sha":"63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63"}],"sha":"1dc9b80352b954210db9da05c3f6f819afc3ce82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/1dc9b80352b954210db9da05c3f6f819afc3ce82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T00:49:55Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T00:49:55Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"sonar: address 4 categories of findings (1-4 of 4)\n\nAfter the SonarCloud export pass — 149 issues, 8 vulns, 5 BLOCKERs —\nwork through the four prioritized actions from the analysis.\n\n1. NOSONAR annotations on 3 gosecurity:S5146 BLOCKER false positives\n   (consent, logout, authorize). Each redirect target is validated\n   against the client''s registered redirect_uris allowlist before\n   reaching http.Redirect; SonarCloud''s dataflow can''t see across\n   the validator helpers. Comments explain the upstream gate so a\n   future reader doesn''t think the suppression hides a real bug.\n\n2. Extract FGA type/relation constants (internal/fga/types.go) and\n   in-file scope constants (cmd/docs-api/handlers.go). Replaces the\n   ~12 worth-fixing go:S1192 duplicated literals: type prefixes\n   (TypeUser, TypeFolder, TypeDocument, TypeGroup), relations\n   (RelOwner, RelEditor, RelViewer, RelMember, RelParent), the ISO\n   timestamp format string. Skipped error-message strings — they\n   should stay local per handler. Also touches internal/outbox/\n   translate.go and cmd/docs-api/{handlers,seed_fga}.go.\n\n3. TypeScript readonly props sweep across 11 web/src files (×22\n   typescript:S6759 findings). All component prop types now use\n   Readonly<{...}>. TS strict build still clean (110kb gz).\n\n4. Extract per-subcommand functions in cmd/idp/main.go to drop\n   cognitive complexity (go:S3776). runGroups: 53 → ~10 (split\n   into runGroupsCreate/List/Member/ListMembers; add+remove share\n   one function gated on a bool). runUsers: 31 → ~10 (similar\n   split with promote+demote sharing). New openPool() helper\n   replaces the DATABASE_URL boilerplate in 3 places.\n\nLive CLI smoke: idp users list, idp groups list both still work.\nFull Go test suite + SPA build clean.","tree":{"sha":"5e33acf819996ec1016ccc5361b8a09bc1811c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/5e33acf819996ec1016ccc5361b8a09bc1811c93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDYzZWMzZDExYmFiNmExMTQ1Mjg0Mjg3YzA4ZTQwNjQ0NzYyZjNhNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc","sha":"80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc"}],"sha":"63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/63ec3d11bab6a1145284287c08e40644762f3a63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T00:12:34Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T00:12:34Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"sonar: add SonarCloud issues export script\n\nAdapted from talha2k/sonarqube-issues-export-to-excel. Pulls every\nissue from the SonarCloud project into sonar/sonarqube_issues.xlsx\n(or .csv) for offline review.\n\n- sonar/sonar_export.py: upstream script with one local change —\n  token is optional. Public SonarCloud projects allow anonymous\n  reads on /api/issues/search; we skip the Authorization header\n  when SONAR_TOKEN is empty. Set the token only for private\n  projects or to bypass anonymous rate limits.\n- Makefile: `make sonar-export [FMT=csv]`. Lazy venv setup at\n  sonar/.venv on first run installs requests + pandas + openpyxl.\n- .gitignore: outputs + venv excluded.\n- sonar/README.md: setup + run notes.\n\nVerified live against mhockenbury_identity-provider (public\nSonarCloud project): 149 issues exported, 35KB xlsx.\n\nInitial summary: 5 BLOCKER, 40 CRITICAL, 62 MAJOR, 42 MINOR;\n141 code smells, 8 vulnerabilities. Top rules: shell-script\nwarnings, TS issues in /web, go:S1192 (duplicated literals)\nand go:S3776 (cognitive complexity).","tree":{"sha":"3ef7cac30c2402deaf22407fcff35bd9ca00c840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/3ef7cac30c2402deaf22407fcff35bd9ca00c840"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDgwYzY5ZjZjODVhZmI0MWYzMDVlZjQxMWU5MTQ1YjViMDNlMjY0Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab","sha":"7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab"}],"sha":"80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/80c69f6c85afb41f305ef411e9145b5b03e264cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T21:34:15Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T21:34:15Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"admin: OAuth client management — API + SPA page\n\nBackend\n- internal/clients/store.go: extend Store with List, Create, Update,\n  RotateSecret, Delete. Create + RotateSecret generate 256-bit\n  base64url-encoded secrets and return PLAINTEXT once; only the\n  argon2id hash lands in the DB.\n- internal/http/admin: 6 new endpoints under /admin/api/clients/*.\n  Same auth gates as the rest of the admin API (scope=admin +\n  is_admin). clientCreatedView embeds plaintext_secret on the\n  create + rotate responses; never on subsequent reads.\n\nFrontend (web/src/admin/ClientsAdmin.tsx)\n- Two-column layout: client list + selected detail.\n- Create form (id, type, redirect URIs, scopes).\n- Detail view with Edit (redirect URIs / grants / scopes) +\n  Rotate secret + Delete buttons. Confirm dialogs warn about\n  the consequences (rotate breaks active backends; delete cascades\n  consents).\n- SecretBanner: prominent amber banner on create/rotate showing\n  the plaintext secret with Copy button. Stays until dismissed\n  to make it obvious the secret won''t be retrievable again.\n- Dashboard tile for Clients count (5-up grid now).\n\nNotes / hints baked into the UI\n- Editing scopes doesn''t revoke issued JWTs (until expiry).\n- Removing a redirect URI breaks any session redirected to it.\n- Public clients can''t have a secret; the form switches automatically.\n\nVerified live via curl: full create → get → rotate → update →\ndelete cycle. plaintext_secret only present on create + rotate\nresponses, null on get.\n\n(Bug caught: mixed named/unnamed return type lists in the Store\ninterface confused the parser. Switched to all-unnamed.)","tree":{"sha":"cef079ce4632b5bf44061794ce6f8607337b3286","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/cef079ce4632b5bf44061794ce6f8607337b3286"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDdmN2MxMGM1ZDg0YWJmNDQ5MGQ2NjMxYmY1MzM4NzU2MmE2NGYxYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b","sha":"70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b"}],"sha":"7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7f7c10c5d84abf4490d6631bf53387562a64f1ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T20:53:51Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T20:53:51Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"docs: subproject 2 close-out — retrospective + sweep stale refs\n\nREADME:\n- Status header: in-progress → core complete (all 9 layers + both UIs)\n- §3 API: full endpoint table for IdP (incl. /admin/api/*), docs-api\n  (with permission tier in responses), and the new web/ SPA\n- §3 architecture diagram: add web SPA node, refresh edge labels\n- §3 component responsibilities: include admin API, SPA, grace cache\n- §6 tradeoffs: replace \"no admin UI\" with \"SPA for product surfaces,\n  HTML for protocol pages\"; add new \"refresh-token reuse grace\" entry;\n  rename \"no reuse detection\" → \"Level 2 with reuse grace, no\n  family-graph yet\"\n- §9 run-it-locally: actual current sequence (compose, dev-all, fga\n  init, run binaries, web-dev, smoke scripts, browser)\n- §11 retrospective: filled in. Maps every primary objective + named\n  gap to specific files. Lists what surprised vs expected. RFC table\n  with one-line takeaways. Carry-forward ledger of unshipped stretches.\n\ndocs/architecture.md:\n- Components: idp now lists admin JSON API; outbox-worker mentions\n  per-tuple coalescing; docs-api mentions permission-tier enrichment +\n  the aud=client_id lab shortcut; new sections for the admin API,\n  the refresh grace cache, and the web SPA; OpenFGA section pinned\n  to v1.14.2 with explanation of the >=1.10 dependency\n\ndocs/learning_objectives.md:\n- Add status banner: 4/4 primary, 3/4 named gaps done\n- Each objective marked ✓ with file paths + test names that verify it\n- Replace \"Client app / SPA integration\" deferred-stretch text with\n  the actual shipped reality\n\ndocs/tradeoffs.md:\n- Resolved-in-§6 list updated\n- KeyResolver split: name internal/jwks.Cache as the actual downstream impl\n- New entries: refresh-token reuse grace, dual-layer admin scope gate,\n  admin API redirect URI shortcut, docs-api aud=client_id shortcut\n- Pending list: refresh family-graph promoted to \"co-exists with grace\n  window cleanly\"; remove \"outbox batch size\" (resolved at 100)\n\nNo code changes; build + vet + tests still green.","tree":{"sha":"80112c43d68a91f69c9824c1de1a22d41fff8329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/80112c43d68a91f69c9824c1de1a22d41fff8329"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDcwZmM1YmQ4NmVlNjRhMDdjNzVkYWQ3NWU4NmY4MGJjOWM0ZjliMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be","sha":"44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be"}],"sha":"70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/70fc5bd86ee64a07c75dad75e86f80bc9c4f9b0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T20:22:34Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T20:22:34Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"oauth: refresh-token reuse grace window (30s)\n\nWhen a refresh token is presented twice within 30s of being rotated\n(typical browser SPA race: parallel renewal calls from React Strict\nMode double-mount, tab refocus mid-renewal, network retries), return\nthe cached response from the first call instead of invalid_grant.\n\nPattern documented by Okta/Auth0 as the way to make rotating refresh\ntokens robust against real-world client races. OAuth 2.1 BCP allows it\nwhen the window is short and bounded.\n\n- internal/oauth/refresh_grace.go: in-memory TTL map keyed by\n  sha256(plaintext). Lazy eviction on access + opportunistic during Put.\n- handleRefresh: cache lookup before Rotate; on success marshal once\n  and Put before writing the response.\n- writeTokenResponseRaw: writes a pre-marshaled body bytewise so the\n  duplicate call gets the same access_token + refresh_token.\n\nIn-memory only (no DB column / KEK encryption) — a 30s window through\nan IdP restart is rare and the worst case is one client gets\ninvalid_grant and re-auths.\n\nVerified live: 2 parallel + 1 sequential /token call with the same\nrefresh_token all return 200 with byte-identical responses\n(matching IdP log: 3× POST /token status:200 bytes:1208).\n\n5 unit tests for the cache primitive (hit, miss, hash isolation,\ncopy-on-Put, expiry eviction).","tree":{"sha":"a6fbe242e7391ed15c3a16a11a788b49b7ce1925","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/a6fbe242e7391ed15c3a16a11a788b49b7ce1925"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDQ0Y2IyNmNhMTU0ZGIyZTljMzg2NWMxMDJhNmM0NGFiOTJmY2Y2YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3","sha":"d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3"}],"sha":"44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/44cb26ca154db2e9c3865c102a6c44ab92fcf6be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T19:47:44Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T19:47:44Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"web: admin UI — dashboard, users, groups, outbox\n\nCompletes the IdP product surface (#13). All four admin pages\nconsume the admin JSON API (#15) via the same Vite proxy.\n\n- auth: SCOPES const always includes ''admin'' (IdP drops it at\n  consent for non-admins, no error path needed). useHasScope\n  hook decodes token scope claim; Layout hides the admin nav\n  link when absent.\n- /admin/  Dashboard — 4 parallel-fetched tiles via useQueries\n- /admin/users — table + inline create form + promote/demote.\n  Self-demote disabled (you-badge in the row)\n- /admin/groups — two-column: group list + member panel with\n  add (email or UUID) + remove. Membership writes go through\n  the outbox, observable in the next page\n- /admin/outbox — pending/failed/all filter tabs (URL-synced\n  via useSearchParams), status pills, expandable payload +\n  last_error. Retry + Purge with two-step confirm. Purge auto-\n  passes force=1 for still-pending rows\n- AdminLayout shows a friendly \"admin access required\" message\n  instead of letting API calls 403 — better UX for non-admins\n  who navigate to /admin directly\n\nBuild clean: 93 modules, 110kb gz. Vite proxy verified live\n(unauth /api/admin/users → IdP 401 through proxy).","tree":{"sha":"e18348939f5b26fd0ba606aa08317dd01f3491bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/e18348939f5b26fd0ba606aa08317dd01f3491bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGQ0NWE3MzdlNDQ0OGEwMzZmM2ZkMzQ2MTBmODZiY2RmODM5ZmM4YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327","sha":"2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327"}],"sha":"d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/d45a737e4448a036f3fd34610f86bcdf839fc8a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-25T19:42:44Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-25T19:42:44Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"idp: admin JSON API + admin scope + is_admin user flag\n\nBackend stretch (#15). Sets up everything the admin SPA needs:\n\n- migration 0003: is_admin BOOL on users (default false)\n- users.Store: IsAdmin field, List() + SetAdmin() methods\n- idp users {list,promote,demote}: CLI surface for the flag\n- consent: silently drops ''admin'' scope when user is_admin=false\n  (logged for observability — a user requesting admin without\n  the flag gets a token without admin in scope, not an error page)\n- internal/http/admin: new package\n  * Authenticate(verifier, store): bearer + scope=admin + is_admin=true\n    triple check. defense-in-depth against post-issue demotion\n  * Handler: 11 endpoints under /admin/api — users (list/create/\n    promote/demote), groups (list/create/members crud), outbox\n    (list/retry/purge with same guards as the CLI)\n- discovery: ''admin:users'' → ''admin'' (single scope name)\n- localdev client: allowed_scopes updated\n- Reuses selfVerifier from layer 7 — no JWKS HTTP fetch needed\n  for the IdP to verify its own tokens\n\nBugs caught live:\n- pgx can''t scan timestamptz into *string. Outbox handler now\n  scans into time.Time / *time.Time and formats in code.\n\nVerified end-to-end: 401 no-token, 403 no-scope, 403 demoted-after-\nissue, 200 happy path. Group create + member add → outbox row\nlands. consent gate dropping ''admin'' confirmed via log line.\n\n5 unit tests in internal/http/admin covering all four auth paths.","tree":{"sha":"b73ea91b8a702cf4b5cc543e06ac43755950367c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/b73ea91b8a702cf4b5cc543e06ac43755950367c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDJjODI5MTExOTE2OWU4MjM4ZWI4NzU4MzUzZTRjNTc5NDkzMzMzMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba","sha":"bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba"}],"sha":"2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/2c8291119169e8238eb8758353e4c57949333327"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:47:08Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:47:08Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"idp: RP-initiated logout — end_session_endpoint + post-logout redirect\n\n- discovery: advertise end_session_endpoint so OIDC client libs find it.\n  Previously oidc-client-ts'' signoutRedirect() aborted because the\n  library couldn''t discover the endpoint.\n- /logout: accept post_logout_redirect_uri + client_id + state (either\n  GET or POST). Validates the URI against the client''s registered\n  redirect_uris (lab shortcut — production would use a separate\n  post_logout_redirect_uris allowlist). Falls back to \"/\" on any\n  mismatch. Echoes state OIDC-style.\n- seed_client.sql: register http://localhost:5173/ so the SPA''s\n  post-logout redirect validates.\n\nVerified live: SPA Sign Out → /logout clears session + bounces back\nto the landing page with state round-tripped.","tree":{"sha":"3618abbc8d858427058ca9514ab41647822db27b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/3618abbc8d858427058ca9514ab41647822db27b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGJjMjc0ODhlNThmNWY4YzVlMTE4ZWVlZjgwOGQ4YTRlNzlmMDk1YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755","sha":"6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755"}],"sha":"bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/bc27488e58f5f8c5e118eeef808d8a4e79f095ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:39:57Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:39:57Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"web: docs SPA (Vite + React + TS) + IdP/docs-api CORS\n\nSPA (/web) — complete docs product surface:\n- Vite 8 + React 19 + TS strict + Tailwind v4 + React Router v7\n- react-oidc-context for auth-code+PKCE against the IdP\n- TanStack Query for server state + mutation cache invalidation\n- Dev proxy: /api/docs → :8083, /api/admin → :8080/admin/api\n- Routes: / (landing), /callback, /docs (list), /docs/:id (detail +\n  edit/delete), /docs/folders/:id, /admin (stub for task 15)\n- Sidebar with folder tree (nested, parent_id walk), permission\n  badges (owner/editor/viewer) everywhere, Edit/Delete buttons\n  gated by canEdit()/canDelete() helpers\n- In-memory token storage only (no localStorage/sessionStorage)\n\ndocs-api enrichment:\n- Responses now include {permission: \"owner\"|\"editor\"|\"viewer\"}\n  computed via up-to-3 FGA Checks, highest-first short-circuit\n- New GET /folders endpoint for the sidebar\n- ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var + go-chi/cors middleware\n\nIdP CORS:\n- /.well-known/*, /token, /userinfo now CORS-enabled via\n  ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var. /authorize + /login stay uncovered\n  (they''re top-level navigations, not XHR).\n- Caught by live browser test: oidc-client-ts fetches discovery\n  before redirecting, needs CORS to succeed.\n\nMakefile: web-install, web-dev, web-build targets. test target\nscoped to ./cmd/... ./internal/... (web/node_modules ships a\nrogue Go file in `flatted` that ./... would walk into).","tree":{"sha":"a1f1bdd3a8688cba897a71a8f10eb189807b7217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/a1f1bdd3a8688cba897a71a8f10eb189807b7217"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDZmNWYwMDBlOTFhYWM5MTg0ZTQ4NjRmNTU5M2UwYzc1Y2Q1YjA3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc","sha":"10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc"}],"sha":"6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6f5f000e91aac9184e4864f5593e0c75cd5b0755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:07:03Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T23:07:03Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"layer 9: docs-api (renamed demo-api), JWKS cache, FGA-gated endpoints\n\n- internal/jwks: HTTP-fetched JWKS cache with per-issuer state,\n  rotation-aware (unknown kid triggers refetch), TTL + stale-if-error,\n  implements tokens.KeyResolver. 6 tests including a full verifier\n  integration that mints + validates a real EdDSA JWT.\n- cmd/docs-api: new binary on :8083 (:8082 is OpenFGA gRPC).\n  authenticate+requireScope middleware, 7 resource endpoints (docs +\n  folders) gated by FGA Check. 404-not-403 when lacking viewer\n  permission so we don''t leak existence.\n- In-memory doc corpus (corpus.go) + deterministic FGA seed (seed_fga.go)\n  built to exercise: direct viewer, inherited viewer via folder parent,\n  editor implies viewer, no-access path. Seed idempotent via\n  OnDuplicateWrites=ignore.\n- scripts/docs_smoke.sh: end-to-end smoke test drives the full auth-code\n  flow + hits every endpoint. Validated live: alice sees 4 docs, 1 is\n  correctly hidden via 404, PATCH works with write:docs scope.\n- Global rename demo-api → docs-api to cohere as a \"docs product\"\n  surface in anticipation of the SPA stretch.\n\nCaveat documented: IdP issues aud=<client_id>, so docs-api must run\nwith REQUIRED_AUD=localdev for local dev. Production IdPs would use\nper-resource audiences or RFC 8707 resource indicators.","tree":{"sha":"38f54c2014379165ee051423df8ceb2a73f35d4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/38f54c2014379165ee051423df8ceb2a73f35d4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDEwYjg3N2I4OWFjNTQyZmNlNGExZmE0OTg3ZGVlMjVhYWVmMjExZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0","sha":"9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0"}],"sha":"10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/10b877b89ac542fce4a1fa4987dee25aaef211fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T22:32:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T22:32:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"outbox 8d-8f: worker + admin CLI + live end-to-end FGA sync\n\n- cmd/outbox-worker: SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED claim, per-tuple\n  coalescing across a batch (W+D on the same key → no-op, fixes the\n  cannot_allow_duplicate_tuples_in_one_request error), atomic ack,\n  attempt_count poison-pill cap, SIGTERM-graceful drain\n- idp outbox {list,retry,purge}: admin CLI over fga_outbox.\n  purge guards against deleting pending rows without --force (common\n  mistake — silently desyncs identity vs FGA)\n- fga.WriteAndDelete: idempotent=true wires OnDuplicateWrites +\n  OnMissingDeletes = ignore so the worker can safely retry\n- docker-compose: OpenFGA v1.9.4 → v1.14.2 (v1.10+ honors the\n  on_duplicate/on_missing flags the SDK sends)\n- .env.example: document OUTBOX_BATCH_SIZE / OUTBOX_POLL_INTERVAL /\n  OUTBOX_MAX_ATTEMPTS\n\nVerified end-to-end: idp groups add-member → outbox pending → worker\ndrain (writes=1) → FGA Check returns allowed:true. Remove path symmetric.","tree":{"sha":"99292693ae7d44a8211a289c846a1adfa1bb8ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/99292693ae7d44a8211a289c846a1adfa1bb8ab4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDk0NDNkMzhkYWE3ZWNiMzZlOTcwYzBhMWM3MDViOGM3OTk3MWFhZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856","sha":"b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856"}],"sha":"9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/9443d38daa7ecb36e970c0a1c705b8c79971aae0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T21:38:33Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T21:38:33Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"outbox 8c: OpenFGA SDK client + idp fga init + authorization model\n\nBrings OpenFGA into the stack. `idp fga init` creates a store, uploads\nthe authorization model (embedded DSL), and prints the IDs for the\noperator to copy into .env. Worker (8d) will use the printed store ID\nto write tuples; demo-api (9) will use it for Check calls.\n\nmigrations/fga/ removed; internal/fga/model.fga is canonical\n  go:embed can''t traverse across module boundaries, so the DSL needs\n  to live inside the Go package that embeds it. Single source of truth.\n\ninternal/fga/model.fga — authorization model\n  4 types: user, group, folder, document\n  folder + document both have: parent, owner, editor, viewer\n  Inheritance via \"editor from parent\" + \"viewer from parent\"\n  Group-based grants via \"[user, group#member]\" on editor/viewer\n  Intentionally NO admin role or negation — stretch items in notes\n\ninternal/fga/model.go\n  Embeds model.fga via go:embed. Exports ModelDSL() + LoadModelFromFile.\n\ninternal/fga/client.go\n  Thin wrapper over openfga/go-sdk + openfga/language DSL transformer.\n  NewClient(Config) — constructs SDK client from env-driven config\n  CreateStore — one-shot at bootstrap\n  UploadModelFromDSL — parses DSL via openfga/language, uploads\n  WriteTuples / WriteAndDelete — batched atomic tuple ops\n  Check — bool-returning wrapper the demo-api will use\n  TupleWithoutCondition — converts between the two tuple shapes the\n    SDK exposes (Write takes ClientTupleKey with optional Condition;\n    Delete takes ClientTupleKeyWithoutCondition). For our\n    no-conditions use case, a trivial projection.\n\ncmd/idp fga init\n  Minimal 50-line subcommand. Creates store + uploads model + prints\n  OPENFGA_STORE_ID and OPENFGA_AUTHORIZATION_MODEL_ID. Not idempotent\n  on purpose — each call creates a fresh store. make dev-all\n  orchestration (8f) will gate on \"do we already have OPENFGA_STORE_ID\n  in env\" before invoking this.\n\n.env.example committed — template documenting every env var the IdP\nexpects. Secrets are <placeholder> values; real values come from\nmake dev-secrets (KEK + CSRF) and idp fga init (store + model IDs).\n\nEnd-to-end live verification:\n  idp fga init → store 01KPV... + model 01KPV...\n  Direct curl to /stores/<id>/authorization-models/<id> → shows all\n    4 types (user, group, folder, document) uploaded correctly\n  Manually wrote: group:editors#member as editor of folder:engineering,\n    document:spec as parent of folder:engineering, user:alice as\n    member of group:editors\n  Check(alice, editor, doc:spec) → allowed: true (2-hop inheritance)\n  Check(alice, viewer, doc:spec) → allowed: true (via editor)\n  Check(bob, editor, doc:spec) → allowed: false (not in group)\n\nDeps added:\n  github.com/openfga/go-sdk v0.8.0 + client subpackage (driven by 8a)\n  github.com/openfga/language/pkg/go/transformer (DSL parser)","tree":{"sha":"b16bd3fb7012b13b7c7a33d59affea384ee9bd5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/b16bd3fb7012b13b7c7a33d59affea384ee9bd5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGI3MmY3MTRhNGQ5M2Q2OGQ3YzNiYTM2NWNhYjM2MTZhNjUzNTk4NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282","sha":"3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282"}],"sha":"b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b72f714a4d93d68d7c3ba365cab3616a65359856"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T20:58:11Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T20:58:11Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"outbox 8b: Enqueue + groups CLI with atomic tx commits\n\nLayer 8''s producer side. CLI-driven group + membership management\ncommits the identity row and the outbox event row in one Postgres\ntransaction — the critical atomicity guarantee that makes the outbox\npattern safe. No ghost events pointing at state that never existed.\n\ninternal/outbox/store.go\n- Enqueue(ctx, tx, event) — single function. Takes pgx.Tx, not a pool.\n  Marshals event.Payload() to JSON, INSERTs into fga_outbox.\n- The pgx.Tx signature is deliberate: you CANNOT Enqueue outside a\n  transaction. Compile-time enforcement of \"always inside a tx.\"\n\nTests (5 integration, all pass):\n- Commit writes the row with pending status, payload JSON round-trips\n  through FromPayload\n- Rollback leaves no row — asserts the core safety property\n- Both event types work identically\n- Context cancellation aborts cleanly\n- Fresh pool (schema present) works — sanity check against dropped\n  migration state\n\ninternal/users/groups.go — first real users of Enqueue\n\nGroupStore with Create, Get{ByID,ByName}, List, AddMemberTx,\nRemoveMemberTx, ListMembers. Tx-accepting methods for membership\nchanges because those MUST run inside the caller''s tx alongside\noutbox.Enqueue.\n\nSentinel errors (ErrGroupNotFound, ErrGroupNameTaken,\nErrMembershipExists, ErrMembershipNotFound) map FK violations and\nuniqueness violations to meaningful types. FK violation on insert →\nErrGroupNotFound because the most common CLI mistake is typing a\nnonexistent group name.\n\nTests (10 integration, all pass):\n- Create + roundtrip via GetByID + GetByName\n- Duplicate name → ErrGroupNameTaken\n- Empty name → error\n- Unknown group → ErrGroupNotFound\n- Add then remove member, assert via ListMembers\n- Duplicate add → ErrMembershipExists\n- Remove nonexistent member → ErrMembershipNotFound\n- Add to unknown group → ErrGroupNotFound (FK violation)\n- List groups\n\ncmd/idp groups — the CLI surface\n\nFive subcommands:\n  groups create <name>\n  groups list\n  groups add-member <group-name> <user-email>\n  groups remove-member <group-name> <user-email>\n  groups list-members <group-name>\n\nGroups referenced by NAME, users by EMAIL — human-readable, not UUIDs.\nEach mutation subcommand resolves both, opens a pgx.Tx, calls\nAddMemberTx or RemoveMemberTx, then Enqueue, then Commit. Uses\ndefer tx.Rollback() as a no-op-after-commit safety net.\n\nEnd-to-end smoke-tested live:\n  idp groups create editors            → group row exists\n  idp groups add-member editors alice  → membership row + pending outbox row\n  idp groups list-members editors      → shows alice\n  idp groups remove-member editors alice → membership gone + 2nd pending outbox row\nBoth outbox rows pending (processed_at NULL), waiting for worker.\n\nIntegration tests now assert the invariant the tests in 8a couldn''t:\nthe outbox row and the identity row commit atomically.","tree":{"sha":"91622c8139ac94538504a93efcdc1d55327f35ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/91622c8139ac94538504a93efcdc1d55327f35ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDNkMWU4NDA3M2I1ZTQ0MjlhZGVjOTY3NTk0MWZiYjQ0MmFlM2QyODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c","sha":"c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c"}],"sha":"3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/3d1e84073b5e4429adec9675941fbb442ae3d282"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T20:27:22Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T20:27:22Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"outbox 8a: event types + translation layer to FGA tuples\n\nFirst piece of layer 8. Pure package — no DB, no HTTP — so the\nshape is testable in isolation before we wire the DB-backed writer\n(8b) and the worker consumer (8d).\n\ninternal/outbox/events.go\n- EventType enum: group_membership_added, group_membership_removed.\n  Deliberately minimal; future events (documents, folders, etc.)\n  extend this list.\n- Event interface with Type() + Payload() methods. Kept tiny; all\n  behavior lives in Translate + FromPayload, not on event values.\n- Typed event structs (GroupMembershipAdded, GroupMembershipRemoved)\n  with uuid.UUID fields — compile-time protection against malformed\n  events.\n- FromPayload(type, raw) rehydrates events the worker reads out of\n  the outbox table. Uses explicit type switch rather than reflection-\n  based auto-registration so adding a new Event without a Decoder\n  is visible in review.\n\ninternal/outbox/translate.go\n- Translate(event) → []TupleOp. Pure function.\n- TupleOp wraps openfga/go-sdk''s ClientTupleKey (we agreed earlier\n  to use SDK types directly rather than a parallel tuple struct —\n  thin translation layer, no impedance mismatch at the FGA boundary).\n- GroupMembershipAdded → write (user:<id>, member, group:<id>).\n- GroupMembershipRemoved → delete (user:<id>, member, group:<id>).\n- Unknown event type → error, not silent no-op. If Translate ever\n  sees an event it can''t handle, that''s a code bug — extend the\n  switch.\n\nTests (14 all pass):\n- Type() + Payload() correctness for both events\n- FromPayload round-trip for both (pairs with Payload() so the\n  outbox store''s marshal+unmarshal path is covered end-to-end)\n- FromPayload rejects unknown types, bad JSON, malformed UUIDs\n- Translate produces expected tuple shape for both events\n- Add + Remove produce identical tuples modulo Kind (so delete\n  actually matches the earlier write)\n- Translate errors on unknown event types\n- Tuple format pinned at \"user:<uuid>\" and \"group:<uuid>\" —\n  reformatting is a breaking change for stored tuples; the test\n  fails visibly if someone \"improves\" the format\n\nDep added: github.com/openfga/go-sdk v0.8.0 + client subpackage.\nTranslation uses client.ClientTupleKey (alias for openfga.TupleKey).\n\nDropped internal/outbox/doc.go — events.go now carries the package\ndoc comment.","tree":{"sha":"be8a2217148d261f37b2aa0460f0ac080a151253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/be8a2217148d261f37b2aa0460f0ac080a151253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGM4NjAxZTdkOGNmNzA4OWU1OTAxZjRjMzQ1MDJhZWZhYjFiYjQzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba","sha":"f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba"}],"sha":"c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/c8601e7d8cf7089e5901f4c34502aefab1bb438c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:45:25Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:45:25Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Capture client-app/SPA integration as a stretch goal\n\nTriggered by the \"browser lands on Unable to connect after consent\"\nobservation. That behavior is correct — /authorize''s 302 to\nhttp://localhost:5173/callback is where the client app WOULD pick up\nthe code, and no client exists. Documented it explicitly in two places\nso it''s clear what''s happening and why.\n\ndocs/learning_objectives.md\n- New \"Client application / SPA integration\" entry under Secondary\n  Objectives. Two escalating implementation options:\n  * Lightweight: tiny catch-all callback listener on :5173 that\n    renders code + state + a ready-to-run /token curl (~30 lines)\n  * Full: real SPA with oidc-client-ts doing browser-side PKCE,\n    token storage, refresh, /userinfo calls\n  Includes the rationale — a client-app companion would turn the\n  subproject into a demonstrably complete OIDC ecosystem rather than\n  just the IdP side.\n\nnotes.md\n- Added \"client-app/SPA integration\" to the Pending stretches line\n  so a fresh session sees it alongside WebAuthn, DPoP, etc.\n\nNo code changes. The browser-flow dead-end is now documented as\nexpected behavior rather than a defect.","tree":{"sha":"aafea82920f198f583e4348d5488e96ac4f33504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/aafea82920f198f583e4348d5488e96ac4f33504"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGY3NmNiN2VhNzY5MTU5NzZkZGY5NjE1M2I4MGE3NDNjOTJiNGI4YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0","sha":"e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0"}],"sha":"f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/f76cb7ea76915976ddf96153b80a743c92b4b8ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:32:04Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:32:04Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add / landing page + /logout to stop dead-ending on post-login\n\nFix for the \"login submits and I get 404\" paper cut. Root cause: login\nredirects to return_to or falls back to \"/\" on empty. No handler was\nregistered at \"/\", so chi''s NotFound served 404. That''s surprising UX\nfor someone who navigates directly to http://localhost:8080/ — which\nis a reasonable thing to do when poking at a server.\n\nOption A per the conversation: a small HTML landing page at / that\nshows login state + a list of protocol endpoints. Companion /logout\nadded because the landing page links to it.\n\ninternal/http/index.go + templates/index.html\n- GET / renders a small HTML page via html/template. Shows either\n  \"Signed in as <email>\" (with logout link) or \"Not signed in\".\n- Lists protocol endpoints with one-liners about each, including\n  the \"/authorize needs params; use `make oauth-url`\" hint.\n- no-store cache-control (login state changes between requests).\n- Path check `r.URL.Path != \"/\"` returns 404 so a /foo routed here\n  by NotFoundHandler in the future doesn''t render the landing page.\n\ninternal/http/logout.go\n- GET or POST /logout deletes the session row + clears the cookie\n  + 302 to /. Idempotent: no-session is a valid no-op that still\n  clears any stale cookie.\n- Accepts GET deliberately — CSRF doesn''t meaningfully protect\n  logout (nothing an attacker gains from forcing someone out\n  beyond annoyance), and <a href> links are convenient.\n- Session.Delete failure is non-fatal: we still clear the cookie;\n  the stale row ages out on its own TTL.\n\ninternal/http/router.go — new Index + Logout handler fields on\nRouterConfig, registered alongside the other session-aware routes\ninside the Sessions != nil guard.\n\ncmd/idp — wires myhttp.Index + myhttp.Logout with userStore +\nsessionStore.\n\nTests (7 new, all pass):\n- Index: anonymous renders \"Not signed in\", logged-in renders email,\n  non-root path 404s, no-store cache-control\n- Logout: redirects to /, deletes session row + clears cookie,\n  no-session still 302s, accepts POST as well as GET\n\nLive smoke-tested:\n- GET / anonymous → \"Not signed in\"\n- make dev-flow still passes (state match, full auth code + token exchange)\n- GET / with post-flow cookie → \"Signed in as smoke-alice@example.com\"\n- GET /logout → 302, cookie cleared, subsequent GET / → \"Not signed in\"","tree":{"sha":"310e9472570baf95349e55db51bb3b740542d1f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/310e9472570baf95349e55db51bb3b740542d1f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGU2ZGI3MTE4MjhhNTA1OGQxNDJhMTM0YzY2ODZjMWM3ZDA1NTkzZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87","sha":"5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87"}],"sha":"e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/e6db711828a5058d142a134c6686c1c7d05593e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:14:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:14:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add missing Makefile targets: up-idp-only, check-deps-idp\n\nBoth were in .PHONY and referenced as prerequisites by dev-reset,\ndev-key, dev-user, dev-serve — but neither target body existed.\nmake silently accepts a missing target as \"Nothing to be done\"\nrather than erroring, so the dev-* chain appeared to work but\nwas bypassing the health check.\n\nup-idp-only brings up just postgres-idp with a wait-for-healthy\nloop. Layer 1–7 work doesn''t need postgres-fga or openfga, so\nrequiring the full compose stack for the dev loop was wasteful.\n\ncheck-deps-idp is the narrower companion to check-deps: verifies\nonly postgres-idp is healthy. All dev-* targets now actually fail\nfast on a missing DB instead of silently no-op''ing.\n\nVerified end-to-end from a fully-down state:\n  make down → make up-idp-only → make migrate → make dev-all\nAll steps actually run and produce expected output.","tree":{"sha":"a3eb745ca6a4352997711bc2c1c1e7994250913e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/a3eb745ca6a4352997711bc2c1c1e7994250913e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDViNDdjZDM0ODZlMWU3YWRlNGQxYWYzM2M0ZTFjMDQxMDJhZmRmODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb","sha":"a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb"}],"sha":"5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/5b47cd3486e1e7ade4d1af33c4e1c04102afdf87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:10:03Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T18:10:03Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Refresh status + subproject docs to reflect layers 1-7 complete\n\nDocs had drifted — README status said \"scaffolding\", notes.md still\nlisted env vars as \"planned\", tradeoffs.md had 8 items under \"pending\"\nthat are all resolved by now.\n\nREADME.md\n- Status line: \"scaffolding — implementation pending\" →\n  \"in progress — OAuth 2.0 + OIDC protocol surface complete (layers\n  1–7). Outbox + FGA wiring pending (layer 8). 16 commits on main.\"\n\nnotes.md\n- New \"Current state\" section with endpoint-to-layer matrix showing\n  every route live end-to-end\n- New \"Decisions (during implementation)\" section capturing the\n  big-pattern choices that emerged during the build:\n  * Ed25519 over RS256; KEK + AES-GCM envelope\n  * Three-state signing key machine + DB-enforced \"one active\"\n  * KeyResolver split (internal direct-DB vs downstream JWKS-cache)\n  * argon2id PHC encoding for passwords + client secrets\n  * Unsigned session cookie, 12h absolute lifetime\n  * Advisory WithSession middleware (not gating)\n  * Plaintext auth codes, hashed refresh tokens\n  * gorilla/csrf + the plaintext-HTTP Referer workaround\n  * RFC 6749 §5.2 error-code collapsing (invalid_grant umbrella)\n- Commands section rewritten around the make dev-* workflow\n- Env vars table split: idp serve (real, with CSRF_KEY added),\n  idp keys/users (real), outbox-worker + demo-api (still planned)\n- All scaffold-era \"open questions\" that got resolved are gone;\n  remaining ones are honestly still open\n\ndocs/tradeoffs.md\n- Moved 8 items from \"Pending\" → \"Resolved during implementation\"\n  with actual implementation notes rather than \"currently leaning\"\n- Added 5 new resolved items that emerged during the build:\n  CSRF plaintext-HTTP workaround, KeyResolver split, OAuth error\n  semantics, auth-code vs refresh storage (plaintext vs hashed),\n  SELECT FOR UPDATE for refresh rotation\n- \"Pending\" now really is pending: outbox batch tuning, RFC 7662\n  introspection, mTLS client auth, DPoP, dynamic client registration,\n  auto-rotation scheduling, KEK rewrap CLI, form_post response mode,\n  rate limiting\n\ndocs/architecture.md\n- Fix factual drift: cookie is UNSIGNED (not signed — the doc originally\n  described what a production IdP would do, not what we built)\n- Fix port: demo-api will be :8082 (OpenFGA occupies host :8081 per\n  compose)\n\nbrain/projects/research/sysdesign-lab/status.md\n- Current State: completely rewritten to reflect 16 commits + layer 7\n  complete\n- New \"Done (identity-provider, layers 1–7)\" section with per-layer\n  summary mirroring the subproject notes.md matrix\n- Next Actions reordered: outbox (layer 8) → demo-api (layer 9) →\n  retrospective\n- Suggested future work: identity-provider-specific items added\n  (WebAuthn, DPoP, reuse detection, KEK rewrap, /metrics, form_post,\n  rate limiting)\n\nNo code changes; all tests still pass, vet clean.","tree":{"sha":"11fa6806a10eeb62f44a15488e3cef816da2bba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/11fa6806a10eeb62f44a15488e3cef816da2bba8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGEzYjUyNzlmOTg5YzIxNTgwMDk0MGQzZWQ4MGZiYTVjNmJkYWI0Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e","sha":"492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e"}],"sha":"a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/a3b5279f989c215800940d3ed80fba5c6bdab4cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T01:19:11Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T01:19:11Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Wire GET /userinfo with scope-filtered claims (layer 7)\n\nOIDC Core §5.3 endpoint. Bearer-authenticated, no session, no CSRF.\nReturns JSON user claims filtered by the scopes in the presented access\ntoken.\n\ninternal/oidc/userinfo.go\n\nHandler flow:\n  1. Extract Authorization: Bearer <token>. Missing or malformed →\n     401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer (no error= per RFC 6750 §3).\n  2. Verify JWT signature + exp + iss via injected TokenVerifier.\n     Bad token → 401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error=\"invalid_token\".\n  3. Require \"openid\" scope. Missing → 403 + WWW-Authenticate:\n     Bearer error=\"insufficient_scope\" scope=\"openid\".\n  4. Parse sub as UUID, look up user. Unknown → 401 invalid_token\n     (don''t leak existence; treat as token no longer valid).\n  5. Build response: sub always; email + email_verified when the\n     token''s scope claim contains \"email\". Cache-Control: no-store.\n\nCase-insensitive scheme match per RFC 6750 §2.1 — \"bearer foo\" also\naccepted. writeBearerChallenge handles WWW-Authenticate quoted-string\nescaping per RFC 7235 §2.1.\n\nTests (14 subtests, all pass, DB-free via fakes):\n- Happy path: openid-only returns sub and nothing else\n- Email scope populates email + email_verified\n- Missing Authorization header → 401, no error= field\n- Malformed Authorization header (5 variants) → 401\n- Invalid token via verifier → 401 + error=\"invalid_token\"\n- Lowercase \"bearer\" accepted\n- Missing openid scope → 403 + insufficient_scope + scope=\"openid\"\n- Unparseable sub → 401 (defensive; shouldn''t happen with valid sig)\n- User lookup fails → 401 (treat as invalid, don''t leak existence)\n- Response Cache-Control: no-store\n\ninternal/tokens/keys.go — new KeyStoreResolver\n\nAdapter: *KeyStore → KeyResolver interface used by *Verifier. Lets the\nIdP verify its OWN access tokens without HTTP round-trips through its\npublic JWKS endpoint. Demo-api (future) will implement KeyResolver\ndifferently, with an HTTP-fetched JWKS cache.\n\nResolves by kid regardless of ACTIVE/PENDING/RETIRED state — retired\nkeys stay resolvable as long as they exist in the table, so access\ntokens signed just before rotation still verify during the overlap\nwindow.\n\ninternal/http/router.go\n\nNew UserInfo http.HandlerFunc field. Registered at GET /userinfo\nindependently of any session or CSRF middleware — bearer is the\ncredential.\n\ncmd/idp serve — wiring\n\nTwo new adapters:\n- userInfoOIDCAdapter: *users.PostgresStore → oidc.UserInfoStore\n  (adds EmailVerified=true for all stored emails; real signup would\n  flip this after email confirmation)\n- selfVerifier: *tokens.Verifier configured with our own issuer URL\n  mapped to a KeyStoreResolver, audience=\"\" to accept tokens issued\n  to any client\n\nscripts/dev_flow.sh — step 8 added\n\nHits /userinfo with the issued access token; pretty-prints the JSON\nresponse. Scope widened from \"openid read:docs\" to \"openid email\nread:docs\" so the email claim is exercised.\n\nEnd-to-end verified:\n  /authorize → /login → /consent → redirect with code →\n  /token exchange → /userinfo with access token →\n  returns {sub, email, email_verified}\n\nID token from the same flow now also carries email + email_verified\n(handler populates when scope includes \"email\").","tree":{"sha":"c3091fbdc3ffb9176dddc923503f3c9f5c680711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/c3091fbdc3ffb9176dddc923503f3c9f5c680711"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDQ5MmQwZGQ0MGIyMzZjN2VkODE5ZWVhOTBkOWY0OWQ2ZmNlYzEwNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562","sha":"0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562"}],"sha":"492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/492d0dd40b236c7ed819eea90d9f49d6fcec106e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:57:23Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:57:23Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Wire POST /token end-to-end (layer 6): auth-code + refresh grants\n\nThe IdP can now complete the full OIDC auth-code + PKCE + refresh\nflow. dev_flow.sh drives everything; browser-based flow also works.\n\ninternal/tokens/refresh.go — opaque refresh-token store\n\nRefresh tokens are 32-byte random strings, base64url-encoded. Unlike\nauth codes (60s TTL, plaintext-in-DB is fine) refresh tokens live\n30 days, so we store a SHA-256 hash — a DB snapshot shouldn''t hand\nan attacker a live credential per row. Hash suffices (not argon2)\nbecause the input is already 256 bits; brute-force resistance is\nnot meaningful.\n\nRotate is the interesting method: BEGIN tx + SELECT FOR UPDATE\nserializes concurrent rotates on the same token, so exactly one\nwins and the rest get ErrRefreshRevoked. Tested with 8 goroutines\nracing to rotate the same token — 1 succeeds, 7 revoked.\n\nScope downgrade allowed (RFC 6749 §6: refresh MAY return a subset).\nScope upgrade rejected (MUST NOT grant new scopes). Both tested.\n\nClient mismatch (token from client A used by client B) maps to\nErrRefreshRevoked rather than a distinct sentinel — avoids leaking\nwhether the token exists.\n\ninternal/oauth/token.go — /token handler\n\nMultiplexes on grant_type: authorization_code + refresh_token.\nClient authentication accepts client_secret_basic (Authorization\nheader) and client_secret_post (form field). Per-grant validation\nshares the invalid_grant sentinel for any of the nominally-distinct\nfailures (unknown code, expired code, revoked refresh, etc.), per\nRFC 6749 §5.2 which intentionally groups them together.\n\nPKCE verification: base64url(SHA-256(verifier)) == stored challenge,\nconstant-time compare. Per RFC 7636 §4.6.\n\nID token issued only when openid scope was requested (OIDC Core\n§3.1.3.3). email + email_verified populated when the email scope\nwas also requested. nonce echoed from the auth_code row (set at\n/authorize time).\n\nRefresh token issued only when client has \"refresh_token\" in its\nAllowedGrants list.\n\nResponse shape matches RFC 6749 §5.1 exactly: access_token,\ntoken_type=Bearer, expires_in, scope, refresh_token, id_token.\nCache-Control: no-store + Pragma: no-cache set on every response\n(including errors) — never cache credentials.\n\nError responses match RFC 6749 §5.2: JSON {error, error_description},\n400 or 401, no redirect (back-channel endpoint).\n\ncmd/idp serve — wiring\n\nTwo new adapters: userInfoAdapter translates *users.PostgresStore\ninto the narrow oauth.UserInfoLookup the token handler needs for\nemail claims. Signer built from the existing keyStore + KEK.\n\nNew env vars with defaults:\n  ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL    default 15m\n  ID_TOKEN_TTL        default 5m\n  REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL   default 720h (30 days)\n\nscripts/dev_flow.sh — extended\n\nNew step 7: POSTs /token with the authorization_code grant, then\nmakes a second call with refresh_token to prove rotation works.\nDecodes both access and ID token payloads (no verify, just\n\"what''s in here\") for a quick sanity pass.\n\nSmoke-tested end-to-end with `make dev-all && make dev-serve &&\nmake dev-flow`:\n- /authorize → /login → POST /login → /consent → POST approve →\n  redirect with code (steps 1-6, from layer 5)\n- POST /token exchanges code for {access_token, id_token, refresh_token}\n- POST /token with refresh_token rotates + returns fresh tokens\n\nDecoded access token shows correct claims: iss, sub (user UUID),\naud=[localdev], exp/nbf/iat, jti, scope, client_id.\nDecoded ID token shows nonce echoed from /authorize, auth_time,\ncorrect aud + sub.\nAccess logs show both POSTs to /token with 200 status.\n\nTests (9 new refresh-store tests, all pass):\n- Issue produces plaintext + row; plaintext NOT in DB\n- Rotate happy path; rotated_from set correctly\n- Old token revoked after rotate (Level 2)\n- Unknown token → ErrRefreshNotFound\n- Wrong client → ErrRefreshRevoked\n- Expired → ErrRefreshExpired\n- Scope subset allowed; scope upgrade rejected\n- Concurrent rotate: 8 goroutines race, 1 wins, 7 revoked\n\nPlus 9 user tests and all other suites still pass.","tree":{"sha":"7ee046c719a548e3b825773b6322a69522c1cd92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/7ee046c719a548e3b825773b6322a69522c1cd92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDBiZTdkMWY2NjIxZTgzNjIzMDU5OTJkNTg0MTg0NjQyYTdkZjI1NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba","sha":"ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba"}],"sha":"0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/0be7d1f6621e8362305992d584184642a7df2562"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:38:59Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:38:59Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Fix another semicolon in auth-code sequence diagram\n\nMissed this one in the previous fix — same class of bug inside the\n/token leg of the auth-code flow diagram.\n\nAlso worth noting: the only Mermaid sequence-diagram lines that need\n<br/> are ones INSIDE the ```mermaid fence. Every other semicolon in\nthe README is plain prose and unaffected.","tree":{"sha":"4bdb13a2a86ef34e689d5306df38ecf84710d3f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/4bdb13a2a86ef34e689d5306df38ecf84710d3f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGFkMTFhZDUzOTI1MTM5MzQ3MGQ5YjJjMDNkYTJjYmRhMTMzYjVlYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981","sha":"961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981"}],"sha":"ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ad11ad539251393470d9b2c03da2cbda133b5eba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:37:40Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:37:40Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Fix Mermaid sequence-diagram parse error (semicolons in message text)\n\nMermaid''s sequence-diagram parser treats semicolons as message terminators,\nso `I->>P: BEGIN tx; INSERT x; COMMIT` blows up with \"Expecting arrow, got\nNEWLINE\" at the first semicolon. The third transaction block in the same\nsection already used <br/> separators correctly; the first two did not.\nNormalized to the same style.\n\nReported by a GitHub Mermaid preview.","tree":{"sha":"a7a0a7ce0f87390fe2412415c876b81cf05ff54b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/a7a0a7ce0f87390fe2412415c876b81cf05ff54b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDk2MWE1YWM3YWZlMmEyMjc3YTEzNzAwZjYzMzk1NGMwMjNiYmY5ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea","sha":"49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea"}],"sha":"961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/961a5ac7afe2a2277a13700f633954c023bbf981"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:36:19Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:36:19Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Wire /authorize end-to-end; add dev loop + OAuth-code flow via curl (5f)\n\nLayer 5 complete: user can walk through /authorize → /login → /consent →\nback to /authorize and receive an authorization code at their client''s\nredirect_uri, all over curl with cookies properly threaded.\n\ninternal/oauth/authorize.go\n\nAuthorize is the protocol integration point that ties 5a-5e together.\nImplements RFC 6749 §4.1.1 + OIDC Core §3.1.2.1:\n\n  1. Validate client_id + redirect_uri via clients.Store. On either\n     failure, render a plain error page — NEVER redirect error info\n     to an untrusted redirect_uri (that''s what an attacker would\n     want us to do).\n  2. Validate remaining params (response_type=code, S256 PKCE,\n     scope ⊆ client.AllowedScopes). From here errors redirect back\n     to the now-trusted redirect_uri with ?error=...&state=... per\n     RFC 6749 §4.1.2.1.\n  3. Session check — if anonymous, pivot to /login?return_to=<self>.\n  4. Consent check — if scopes not on file, pivot to /consent?...\n     passing state so consent POST can bring the user back here.\n  5. Issue code via oauth.AuthCodeStore, redirect to redirect_uri\n     with ?code=...&state=...\n\nHandler depends on narrow interfaces (ClientStore, consent.Store,\nAuthCodeStore, CurrentSessionUser fn) so tests bypass the DB.\nCompile-time check that *clients.PostgresStore satisfies ClientStore.\n\nTests (10 all pass):\n- Happy path issues code + redirects with state; code store sees\n  PKCE challenge, nonce, scopes\n- Missing client_id / unknown client / unregistered redirect_uri →\n  plain 400 (no redirect-based error leak)\n- response_type=token → unsupported_response_type redirect\n- Missing PKCE → invalid_request redirect\n- code_challenge_method=plain → invalid_request redirect\n- Scope exceeds client allow list → invalid_scope redirect\n- No session → /login redirect with return_to\n- No consent → /consent redirect carrying all state for continuation\n\ninternal/http/router.go\n\nLayer-5 routes wired into the chi router under a conditional block\n(nil Sessions field skips the whole set, keeping the minimal\ndiscovery+JWKS boot intact). Middleware chains:\n- /authorize: WithSession\n- /login: CSRF only (POST establishes the session)\n- /consent: WithSession + CSRF\nCompile-time checks that *users.PostgresSessionStore satisfies\nusers.SessionStore and *tokens.KeyStore satisfies oidc.JWKSKeyStore.\n\ncmd/idp\n\nNew subcommand: `idp users create <email> <password>` + `idp users list`.\nNeeded for dev so no hand-crafted SQL + argon2id hash production is\nrequired when seeding test users.\n\nserve wires layer 5: builds storage + handler configs + a\nclientLookupAdapter bridging *clients.PostgresStore to\nmyhttp.ClientLookup (the consent handler''s narrow interface).\nNew env var CSRF_KEY required at boot; fail-fast on missing.\n\n--- Dev loop ---\n\nMakefile dev-* targets for fast iteration without hand-crafting SQL:\n\n  make dev-secrets     # write /tmp/idp-env with fresh KEK + CSRF_KEY\n                         (idempotent; FORCE=1 regenerates)\n  make dev-reset       # TRUNCATE test state, re-seed localdev client\n  make dev-key         # idempotent: generate + activate a signing key\n                         if none active\n  make dev-user        # idempotent: create smoke-alice@example.com /\n                         correct-horse-battery-staple\n  make dev-all         # one-shot: secrets + reset + key + user\n  make dev-serve       # source /tmp/idp-env and run ./bin/idp serve\n  make oauth-url       # print a ready-to-paste /authorize URL with\n                         fresh PKCE challenge + code_verifier\n  make dev-flow        # drive full OAuth code flow via scripts/dev_flow.sh\n\ndev-* targets use check-deps-idp (postgres-idp only) rather than the\nfull check-deps (postgres-idp + postgres-fga + openfga), because\nlayer 5 doesn''t touch FGA. New up-idp-only target brings up just the\nIdP''s Postgres.\n\nscripts/dev_flow.sh drives all 6 flow steps with cookie persistence,\nextracts CSRF tokens from HTML, handles html/template entity encoding\non hidden-field values, asserts state round-trips cleanly, and prints\nthe ready-to-exchange code_verifier + example /token curl (commented\nout until /token is implemented).\n\nSmoke-tested end-to-end — `make dev-all && make dev-serve &&\nmake dev-flow` produces a valid authorization code in ~100ms across\nall 6 HTTP requests, clean shutdown on SIGTERM.\n\nMinor:\n- Fixed an Edit-dance typo: had both net/http and nethttp \"net/http\"\n  imported in cmd/idp/main.go; consolidated to nethttp.\n- Makefile dev-reset initially tried a heredoc — Make recipes run\n  line-by-line so heredocs need .ONESHELL or a single -c string.\n  Used single -c for clarity.","tree":{"sha":"0afd231fcbdfb2338ec85fd0f197ba1352fe8abf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/0afd231fcbdfb2338ec85fd0f197ba1352fe8abf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDQ5NzE1OTIxYWRjYmY2ZTM3NmE1YmJhYjhjMzZlMmRjMGQwMTYzZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869","sha":"025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869"}],"sha":"49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/49715921adcbf6e376a5bbab8c36e2dc0d0163ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:15:14Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:15:14Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add consent store + handler + template (5e)\n\ninternal/consent/store.go\n\nPostgresStore for the consents table. Sorts + dedupes scopes before\nstorage so comparisons are order-independent. HasScopes is a SUBSET\ncheck: requesting a subset of previously-consented scopes passes\nthrough, a superset re-prompts.\n\nTests (8): no-row → false, empty request → vacuously true, grant +\nread back, order-independent, subset passes, superset fails, grant\noverwrites, duplicate inputs deduped.\n\ninternal/http/consent.go + templates/consent.html\n\nGET /consent renders the approve/deny form. Shows client_id, the\nuser''s email, and the requested scopes. Hidden fields carry\nclient_id, redirect_uri, state, return_to, and one <input name=\"scope\">\nper scope so the POST receives everything without re-deriving.\n\nPOST /consent writes the consent row on approve and redirects to\nreturn_to (which /authorize populates with its own URL so it can\nfinish the flow). On deny, redirects to the CLIENT''s redirect_uri\nwith error=access_denied per RFC 6749 §4.1.2.1, carrying state\nthrough.\n\nSecurity properties, each tested:\n- No session → redirect to /login?return_to=<consent URL> so the\n  flow completes after login\n- Unknown client_id → 400\n- redirect_uri not in client''s allow list → 400 (both GET and POST,\n  defense in depth)\n- return_to validated same-origin (reuses validateReturnTo from\n  login.go)\n- CSRF token embedded, verified by middleware chain in router\n- Invalid decision value (not approve/deny) → 400 rather than\n  defaulting either way\n\nA small ClientLookup interface on the ConsentConfig keeps the\npackage from importing *clients.Store. An adapter in the clients\npackage (forthcoming in layer 5f''s /authorize wiring) will satisfy\nthe interface.\n\nTests (8 handler, all pass):\n- GET: no-session → /login redirect, logged-in renders form,\n  unknown client → 400, unregistered redirect_uri → 400\n- POST: approve writes row + 302 to return_to, deny redirects to\n  client with error=access_denied + state, tampered redirect_uri\n  → 400, invalid decision → 400\n\nVet caught a self-assignment `*r = *r` left over from an earlier\niteration of the attachSession test helper; cleaned up.","tree":{"sha":"741970e3882ebb8af76a04235e455031044070b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/741970e3882ebb8af76a04235e455031044070b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDAyNTA2OWQ5NGE3NmNhYmZiYTMwNjNlMjM0NTFjNGYyZDNhMDA4Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b","sha":"b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b"}],"sha":"025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/025069d94a76cabfba3063e23451c4f2d3a00869"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:09:30Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:09:30Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add login handler + templates (5d)\n\nFirst HTML-serving surface. GET /login renders the form; POST /login\nauthenticates + issues session cookie + redirects to return_to.\n\ninternal/http/templates.go\n- html/template (not text/template — context-aware escaping) parsed\n  once at startup from an embed.FS. Fail at boot on template errors;\n  don''t let broken templates hide behind a working server.\n\ninternal/http/templates/login.html\n- Minimal inline CSS so it looks OK in a browser for dev. CSRF token\n  rendered via {{ .CSRFField }}. Email pre-populated on error so the\n  user doesn''t retype.\n\ninternal/http/login.go\n\nLoginGET: renders the form with a CSRF token + any passed return_to.\nLoginPOST: parses form, Authenticate, creates session on success,\nsets cookie, 302 to return_to.\n\nFour deliberate security properties, each tested:\n\n1. Generic error message — \"Invalid email or password\" for BOTH\n   users.ErrNotFound AND users.ErrPasswordMismatch. User enumeration\n   defense. Test TestLoginPOST_NoSuchUserSameResponseAsWrongPassword\n   asserts both paths produce identical status codes and identical\n   .error div contents. (Email echoed back into the form differs\n   between paths, which is intentional UX; the error message itself\n   must not.)\n\n2. return_to open-redirect defense — validateReturnTo accepts only\n   same-origin URLs (comparing scheme+host against BaseURL) OR\n   relative paths starting with /. Absolute URLs are normalized\n   down to path+query for the redirect. Anything cross-origin or\n   without a leading slash becomes \"\", which the handler substitutes\n   with \"/\". Test RejectsCrossOriginReturnTo covers this.\n\n3. Buffered template render — ExecuteTemplate writes to a bytes.Buffer\n   first so a template error produces a clean 500 rather than a\n   half-rendered page with a status line that''s already committed.\n\n4. Cache-Control: no-store on all login responses. The form''s CSRF\n   token is fresh per render and we never want a proxy to serve a\n   stale cached form.\n\nTests (6 all pass):\n- GET renders form with text/html + no-store Cache-Control\n- POST with correct password creates session, sets cookie, 302 to return_to\n- POST with wrong password returns 401 with generic error, no session\n- Wrong password and unknown email produce identical error messages\n- Cross-origin return_to gets dropped to \"/\"\n- Absolute same-origin return_to gets normalized to path+query\n\nFake user store in tests implements users.Store so login.go can be\ntested without a DB. Fake session store is reused from session_test.go.","tree":{"sha":"bbf7cdfcb07656f9bbfde8736587d37d1fca0055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/bbf7cdfcb07656f9bbfde8736587d37d1fca0055"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGIyNDIyNWY2YTNlY2I1ODYzMmRkZDcyYjFhN2U3MDMxZmVmNGM2OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa","sha":"6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa"}],"sha":"b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b24225f6a3ecb58632ddd72b1a7e7031fef4c68b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:07:16Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-22T00:07:16Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add CSRF middleware via gorilla/csrf (5c)\n\ninternal/http/csrf.go\n\nThin wrapper around github.com/gorilla/csrf so our handlers get a\nsingle CSRFMiddleware(authKey, secure) call and templates can embed\nthe token via csrf.TemplateField. POST /login + POST /consent will\nchain this in layers 5d and 5e.\n\nParseCSRFKey validates the 32-byte hex env var shape at startup; the\nserve subcommand calls this so a missing/malformed key fails loudly\nat boot rather than silently at first request.\n\nGotcha found in practice + fixed: gorilla/csrf v1.7.3 enforces a strict\nTLS-oriented Referer check on POSTs that rejects every request in a\nplaintext HTTP deployment. The library offers PlaintextHTTPRequest\nas the escape hatch; when secure=false we apply it before the protect\nmiddleware inspects the request. The referer check is meant to defend\nagainst HTTP-MITM injecting forms into a nominally-TLS site — doesn''t\napply when we''re KNOWN to be plaintext HTTP (lab / localhost).\n\nTests (5 new, all pass):\n- ParseCSRFKey: valid hex round-trip, rejects empty/non-hex/too-short/\n  too-long\n- POST without token → 403\n- GET issues token + cookie, POST with matching token → 200\n- Mismatched-key token from a different CSRFMiddleware instance\n  rejected → 403\n\nDeps added: github.com/gorilla/csrf v1.7.3 + securecookie v1.1.2","tree":{"sha":"c734cd8eb2542709175b4a4fe30b6c925b44560f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/c734cd8eb2542709175b4a4fe30b6c925b44560f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDZlMmMxOGY3ODMwNDI2ZTg5MzI0MzJmNjE1Yjg3NGQwZjNiZWE2ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5","sha":"7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5"}],"sha":"6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/6e2c18f7830426e8932432f615b874d0f3bea6fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:59:59Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:59:59Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add authorization codes store with atomic single-use (5b)\n\ninternal/oauth/codes.go\n\nAuthCodeStore persists the short-lived, single-use codes emitted by\n/authorize and redeemed at /token. Per RFC 6749 §4.1.2: <=60s TTL,\nsingle-use, bound to one client + one redirect_uri, carries PKCE\nchallenge for /token to verify.\n\nIssue mints a 32-byte random code (base64url, no padding → ~43 chars;\ncomfortably over RFC 6749 §10.10''s 128-bit recommendation) and persists\nall the fields /token will need later.\n\nConsume is the interesting one. Pseudo-flow:\n  1. Load the row to read fields (/token needs them) + to distinguish\n     \"not found\" / \"mismatch\" / \"expired\" / \"already used\" cases.\n  2. Atomic claim via UPDATE ... WHERE used_at IS NULL AND expires_at\n     > now() RETURNING used_at. If that affects zero rows, a racing\n     Consume claimed it — return ErrCodeAlreadyUsed.\n\nCrucially, the client_id + redirect_uri mismatch check runs BEFORE\nthe atomic claim. A wrong client/redirect does NOT burn the code,\nso the legitimate holder can still redeem. Tests cover this: wrong\nclient → ErrCodeClientMismatch, then same code + right client\nsucceeds.\n\nStorage choice: plaintext code in DB. Auth codes have brutally short\nTTLs + single-use semantics; hashing would add no meaningful security\nand complicates the lookup path. Refresh tokens (long-lived) WILL hash.\n\nTests (7, all pass, concurrent-safety included):\n- Round-trip Issue → Consume\n- Two Consume calls: second returns ErrCodeAlreadyUsed\n- Wrong client_id → ErrCodeClientMismatch, code stays redeemable\n- Wrong redirect_uri → ErrCodeClientMismatch\n- Expired code → ErrCodeExpired, not marked used\n- Unknown code → ErrCodeNotFound\n- Concurrent Consume: 8 goroutines race, exactly 1 succeeds,\n  7 return ErrCodeAlreadyUsed. Proves the UPDATE ... RETURNING\n  pattern is actually atomic in practice.","tree":{"sha":"c560fc93bb53cef39b770e9c1bb6e02620a5fdf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/c560fc93bb53cef39b770e9c1bb6e02620a5fdf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDdlNzJmYjcyOWE5OTI4ZGNiNzU2MzljZTQzNDkwZTkzM2U3ODFjYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93","sha":"ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93"}],"sha":"7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/7e72fb729a9928dcb75639ce43490e933e781cc5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:55:58Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:55:58Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add session store + cookie + WithSession middleware (5a)\n\nFirst piece of layer 5 (the /authorize flow).\n\ninternal/users/sessions.go\n- PostgresSessionStore with Create/Get/Delete/DeleteExpired against\n  the existing sessions table from migration 0001.\n- Get auto-cleans an expired row on the way out (ErrSessionExpired\n  sentinel + best-effort DELETE). Second Get returns NotFound.\n- DefaultSessionTTL = 12h, absolute lifetime (no sliding extension\n  in this lab).\n\ninternal/http/session.go\n- SetSessionCookie / ClearSessionCookie / ReadSessionCookie —\n  HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax. Secure=true only when ISSUER_URL is https\n  (the handler layer passes that in).\n- WithSession middleware resolves the cookie to a users.Session and\n  attaches it to request context; handlers read it via\n  SessionFromContext. The middleware is ADVISORY, not gating — it\n  populates the context but doesn''t redirect on missing session.\n  /authorize and /consent handle the \"no session\" case themselves\n  (redirect to /login) so the same middleware covers paths with\n  optional sessions too.\n- Stale cookies (session deleted/expired) are treated as anonymous;\n  the middleware does NOT clear them. Intentional: /login on next\n  successful auth overwrites the cookie anyway, and clearing here\n  creates a Set-Cookie on every anonymous request, which would\n  surprise any layer 7 that tried to manage cookies explicitly.\n\nDeliberate simplification: session cookie is UNSIGNED. A forged\nsession ID fails the Postgres lookup, so the security property\n(\"unforgeable session\") holds via DB authority. A real IdP would\nHMAC-sign for defense in depth + to carry additional data without\nDB hits. Flagged in sessions.go package comment.\n\nTests (14 new, all pass):\n- Session store: round-trip, not-found/expired sentinels, expired\n  auto-cleanup, Delete idempotent, DeleteExpired only removes\n  expired.\n- Cookie helpers: round-trip, HttpOnly + SameSite, Secure gate,\n  clear-cookie emits MaxAge<0, missing/malformed cookie errors.\n- Middleware: attaches session to ctx when valid, passes through\n  with nil session when no cookie or when store doesn''t know the\n  id, does NOT clear stale cookies.","tree":{"sha":"2781eb30e44b1f7b4539f522803358a77aadbd20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/2781eb30e44b1f7b4539f522803358a77aadbd20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGVjYWQ3ZTk5Y2ZhMTg0OWUzZDZkMzBkMjU0NjIwNTJhYjIyNDJkOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1","sha":"82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1"}],"sha":"ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/ecad7e99cfa1849e3d6d30d25462052ab2242d93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:44:32Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:44:32Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add OIDC discovery + JWKS + HTTP server skeleton\n\nLayer 4 of the plan. First time cmd/idp actually serves HTTP; exposes\nthe two read-only OIDC endpoints so downstream clients (including\noidc-client-ts in later tests) can discover the IdP''s surface.\n\ninternal/oidc/discovery.go\n- Discovery struct with required + standard-optional fields per\n  OpenID Connect Discovery 1.0 §4, RFC 8414. Emits only what we\n  implement: response_types=[code], alg=[EdDSA], PKCE=[S256],\n  grants=[authorization_code, refresh_token]. Deliberately does NOT\n  advertise implicit/hybrid, HS-family algs, or client_credentials.\n- BuildDiscovery is pure (config → struct) so tests don''t need an\n  HTTP layer. Handler constructs and marshals once at startup.\n- Cache-Control: public, max-age=300 (spec recommends caching; 5min\n  lets issuer URL changes propagate reasonably fast).\n\ninternal/oidc/jwks.go\n- JWKSKeyStore interface — narrow surface the handler actually needs.\n  *tokens.KeyStore satisfies it; tests fake it without a DB.\n- JWKSHandler wraps ForJWKS → BuildJWKS → JSON. Empty key set returns\n  200 with keys:[] (valid state, not an error). DB errors become 500\n  without leaking the error detail. Also 5min Cache-Control.\n\ninternal/http/router.go\n- chi v5 router with middleware stack: RequestID, RealIP, Recoverer,\n  accessLog (our own slog-based structured per-request log),\n  Timeout(10s).\n- Registers /.well-known/openid-configuration, /.well-known/jwks.json,\n  /healthz. Others land in later commits.\n- healthHandler pings Postgres if configured; returns 503 on failure\n  with details in body. Nil-safe.\n- Compile-time check that *tokens.KeyStore implements oidc.JWKSKeyStore\n  so a future refactor can''t silently break the seam.\n\ncmd/idp serve\n- New subcommand. Opens Postgres pool + KEK at startup, boots chi\n  router, blocks on signal.NotifyContext(SIGINT, SIGTERM), then\n  server.Shutdown(SHUTDOWN_GRACE ctx).\n- Startup warns (does not error) if no active signing key — /jwks\n  will serve empty, /token (future) will fail, operator runs\n  `idp keys generate && activate` to fix.\n- Env: DATABASE_URL, JWT_SIGNING_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY (both shared with\n  `keys` subcommand), plus ISSUER_URL, HTTP_ADDR, SHUTDOWN_GRACE,\n  LOG_LEVEL (serve-only). DSN password redacted in logs.\n\nTests (14 new, all pass):\n- Discovery: endpoint-URL derivation, REQUIRED fields present,\n  advertises-only-implemented (no implicit flow, EdDSA only, S256\n  only, code+refresh grants only), handler serves JSON with correct\n  content-type + cache-control. Trailing-slash behavior pinned as\n  explicit (naive concat; documented as future hardening).\n- JWKS: round-trip through handler + tokens.ParseJWKS (downstream\n  contract), empty set returns 200 not 500, store errors become\n  500 without leaking details.\n\nSmoke-tested end-to-end: built binary, generated + activated a key\nvia `idp keys ...`, started `idp serve`, curl''d all three endpoints\n(healthz, discovery, jwks). Discovery doc matches spec shape; JWKS\nexposes our active Ed25519 key with the right kid. Access logs\ninclude request_id + duration. SIGTERM logs \"shutdown signal\nreceived\" → \"shutdown complete\" and exits 0.\n\nDep added: github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.2.5","tree":{"sha":"edb20e915eb9e0e6e41c1a3f2d1af939c00959d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/edb20e915eb9e0e6e41c1a3f2d1af939c00959d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDgyYjdjNWI2NDI0NjU5NTk4ZmU2OGU5YjM0ZmNhMWQwZGExNzMxYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300","sha":"26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300"}],"sha":"82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/82b7c5b6424659598fe68e9b34fca1d0da1731c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:33:55Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:33:55Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add JWT signing + verification + JWKS serialization\n\nLayer 3 of the IdP plan. Builds on the key store from the previous\ncommit; turns signing keys into signed tokens and verifiable tokens\nback into typed claims.\n\ninternal/tokens/claims.go\n- BaseClaims embeds jwt.RegisteredClaims so iss/sub/aud/exp/nbf/iat/jti\n  validation comes for free from jwt-go v5\n- AccessClaims composes BaseClaims + scope (space-separated per RFC 6749\n  §3.3) + client_id\n- IDClaims composes BaseClaims + nonce + auth_time + email/email_verified\n  (OIDC Core §5.3 minimal subset)\n\ninternal/tokens/jwt.go\n- Signer wraps a KeyStore + KEK. SignAccessToken / SignIDToken pick up\n  whatever key is ACTIVE at call time, so rotating mid-flight just\n  changes which key signs subsequent tokens. Header kid matches\n  SigningKey.KID; downstream services look it up in JWKS.\n- fillRegistered populates iss/iat/nbf/exp/jti (signer-controlled);\n  sub/aud are caller-controlled because they vary per-request.\n- Verifier accepts a map of trusted issuers → KeyResolver. An iss not\n  in the allowlist is rejected before any crypto — ErrIssuerMismatch.\n  Audience enforcement: if verifier is configured with an audience,\n  the token''s aud MUST contain it.\n- resolveKey peeks at the unverified claims to find iss, picks the\n  right resolver per-issuer, then jwt-go re-verifies with the\n  resolved key. Typed sentinels for each failure mode:\n  ErrInvalidToken / ErrUnknownKID / ErrUnexpectedAlg /\n  ErrIssuerMismatch / ErrAudienceMissing.\n- Clock is injectable so tests assert exp/nbf without sleeping.\n\ninternal/tokens/jwks.go\n- BuildJWKS serializes []*SigningKey into the RFC 7517 wire format:\n  {\"keys\": [{\"kty\":\"OKP\",\"crv\":\"Ed25519\",\"x\":<b64url>,\"kid\":...,\n   \"use\":\"sig\",\"alg\":\"EdDSA\"}, ...]}. Matches RFC 8037 §2 for Ed25519.\n- ParseJWKS + JWK.PublicKey() for the downstream (demo-api) path,\n  with defensive checks for wrong kty / wrong curve / wrong byte size.\n- BuildJWKS(nil) emits `\"keys\":[]` not `\"keys\":null` — specifically\n  tested; clients don''t expect to handle null.\n\nTests cover the four named learning gaps explicitly:\n\nMulti-issuer validation:\n- TestVerify_AcceptsTokenFromAnyTrustedIssuer — verifier trusts\n  idp-a + idp-b; token from B verifies successfully\n- TestVerify_SameKIDAcrossIssuersResolvedByIssuer — both IdPs\n  advertise the SAME kid string; verifier resolves by issuer first,\n  not by kid. This is the subtle bit tutorials skip.\n- TestVerify_RejectsTokenFromUnknownIssuer — iss not in allowlist\n\nDownstream signature verification:\n- TestVerify_RejectsForgedToken — attacker signs with their own key,\n  claims our kid + iss; verifier looks up the real public key for\n  that kid and the signature check fails\n- TestVerify_UnknownKIDSurfacesAsSentinel — distinct sentinel lets\n  demo-api middleware decide \"refetch JWKS\" (unknown kid) vs\n  \"reject outright\" (invalid sig)\n- TestVerify_RejectsTamperedPayload — flip a byte in the payload\n  segment; signature verify fails\n\nPlus:\n- TestVerify_RejectsExpiredToken (advance clock past exp)\n- TestVerify_RejectsWrongAudience\n- TestVerify_RejectsWrongAlg (HS256 token rejected even though\n  structurally valid)\n- TestSignIDToken_CarriesNonceAndEmail\n- TestSign_NoActiveKeyReturnsError (surfaces the store''s sentinel)\n\nJWKS round-trip tests: shape-per-RFC-7517, empty-array encoding,\nbuild→marshal→parse→extract-pubkey equality, JWK.PublicKey rejects\nwrong kty / wrong curve / malformed X / wrong size.\n\nDesign notes captured in code comments:\n- Why AccessClaims and IDClaims compose rather than alias\n- Why per-request claims stay caller-controlled vs signer-controlled\n- Why the Verifier''s iss allowlist is structured per-issuer-resolver\n- Why retired keys drop from JWKS immediately in this lab (operator\n  enforces overlap window by waiting between rotate and retire)\n\nMulti-issuer tests use a lightweight \"sign directly with jwt-go\"\npattern for the second issuer because the DB-enforced \"at most one\nactive key\" constraint prevents two DB-backed signer fixtures from\ncoexisting. The verifier doesn''t care about provenance — it just\nsees signed JWTs.\n\nDep added: github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 v5.3.1","tree":{"sha":"5f2229203e91e1f198488ed6830d6537fe45cb5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/5f2229203e91e1f198488ed6830d6537fe45cb5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDI2ZWM3YWVkMTM5OTRiZjA1OTgzNzFjOTllNGU4MmY4NDI4ODQzMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9","sha":"84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9"}],"sha":"26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/26ec7aed13994bf0598371c99e4e82f842884300"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:15:01Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:15:01Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add signing-key store + 3-state rotation + keys CLI\n\nEd25519 signing keys persist in the signing_keys table with the\nprivate half wrapped under the KEK (previous commit). The three-state\nmachine — PENDING → ACTIVE → RETIRED — is derived from\n(activated_at, retired_at) timestamps:\n\n  PENDING  activated_at IS NULL  AND  retired_at IS NULL\n  ACTIVE   activated_at NOT NULL AND  retired_at IS NULL    (at most one)\n  RETIRED  activated_at NOT NULL AND  retired_at NOT NULL\n\nDefense in depth on \"at most one active\": migration 0002 adds a\npartial unique index (CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON signing_keys ((1))\nWHERE activated_at IS NOT NULL AND retired_at IS NULL). A race or\ncode bug that tries to activate a second key fails with\nErrKeyAlreadyActive — the DB is the final word, not the application.\n\nKeyStore:\n- Generate   create PENDING row; returns key with plaintext private\n             half already loaded (caller can use immediately if needed)\n- Activate   PENDING → ACTIVE (unique-violation → ErrKeyAlreadyActive)\n- Retire     ACTIVE → RETIRED\n- GetActive  returns sole ACTIVE key, or ErrNoActiveKey\n- GetByID    any state\n- List       all rows, for CLI display (private halves left wrapped)\n- ForJWKS    ACTIVE + PENDING, excludes RETIRED — what appears at\n             /.well-known/jwks.json\n\nSigningKey.Unwrap(kek) decrypts the stored blob into an ed25519\nprivate key; idempotent. PrivateKey() panics on unsealed access\n(programming-error assertion).\n\nCLI in cmd/idp (first real code there):\n  idp keys generate             create pending key\n  idp keys list                 tabwriter table with status + age\n  idp keys activate <kid>       PENDING -> ACTIVE\n  idp keys retire <kid>         ACTIVE  -> RETIRED\nEnv: DATABASE_URL + JWT_SIGNING_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY (64 hex chars).\nHTTP server subcommand will land in a later commit.\n\nTests (11 new, all pass against real Postgres):\n- Generate creates pending with correct fields + Ed25519 key size\n- Wrap/store/reload/Unwrap round-trip produces a working private key\n  (verified by deterministic sign comparison)\n- Activate happy path + second-activation-blocked (ErrKeyAlreadyActive)\n- Full rotation cycle (A active → B pending → A retire → B activate)\n- Can''t reactivate a retired key (one-way state machine)\n- Can''t retire a pending key\n- GetActive returns sentinel when no active\n- ForJWKS excludes retired\n- Pure test of Status() helper (no DB)\n\nBug caught during test authoring: `defer pool.Close()` in tests ran\nBEFORE `t.Cleanup(DELETE ...)` because defer fires before Cleanup\ncallbacks (which run LIFO after defers). Cleanup DELETEs silently\nfailed through a closed pool and test rows leaked across runs.\nFix: register `pool.Close` via `t.Cleanup` too, so the LIFO order\nruns row deletions first, then the close. Same-bug, unfixed in\nurl-shortener''s tests — probably worth flagging as a cross-repo\ncleanup later.\n\nSmoke-tested the CLI end-to-end: generate → activate → second\ngenerate+activate blocked → retire first → activate second →\nfinal list shows both with correct statuses.","tree":{"sha":"f961ef24346bf254d846252f9ed1322e6274a6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/f961ef24346bf254d846252f9ed1322e6274a6ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDg0YTllYjBkYjAwYThjY2ViYTk1Y2ZjZjgxNzNlNDAzODA5ZmIyYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461","sha":"134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461"}],"sha":"84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/84a9eb0db00a8cceba95cfcf8173e403809fb2b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:06:26Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T23:06:26Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add KEK envelope encryption (AES-256-GCM with kid-as-AAD)\n\nThe Key Encryption Key wraps signing-key private halves at rest. In\nproduction this would be a KMS; here it''s an env-var-loaded 32-byte\nsymmetric key. The KEK interface is deliberately small so swapping\nto KMS later changes only the implementation.\n\nDesign notes:\n- AES-256-GCM. kid is bound as AAD so ciphertexts can''t be silently\n  swapped between signing-key rows (cheap defense against row-mix\n  bugs, and the authentication fails loud if it ever happens).\n- Output format is nonce || ciphertext_with_tag. Nonce is fresh per\n  Wrap() call; the \"two wraps of the same plaintext produce different\n  ciphertexts\" property is asserted in tests.\n- Truncated / tampered / wrong-KEK / wrong-kid blobs all return the\n  same ErrCiphertextTampered sentinel; callers shouldn''t distinguish.\n- ErrInvalidKEK on malformed input at load time (wrong length,\n  bad hex).\n\nTests cover: round trip, nonce freshness, wrong-kid fail, wrong-KEK\nfail, ciphertext tamper fail, truncated blob fail, bad hex at load.\n\nExplicit non-goals: KEK rotation (deferred to a stretch CLI\nsubcommand), multi-key keyring (not needed), HSM integration.","tree":{"sha":"583a80b957053ba779232616564b2f109a6bba25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/583a80b957053ba779232616564b2f109a6bba25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDEzNDE0ODkwNGM3ZmEzNDllYzc0ZDUxNmExYmU0NWVhMTI2NTM0NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd","sha":"510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd"}],"sha":"134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/134148904c7fa349ec74d516a1be45ea12653461"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T22:50:10Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T22:50:10Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Add users + clients stores with argon2id password hashing\n\nFirst layer of real code. Pure + integration tests against real\nPostgres (skip-on-unreachable, no mocked DBs).\n\nusers:\n- password.go: HashPassword / VerifyPassword wrapping argon2id in\n  PHC-encoded format ($argon2id$v=19$m=,t=,p=$salt$hash). Params\n  encoded in the hash so verification survives future DefaultArgon2Params\n  bumps without re-hashing. Constant-time compare on verify.\n- store.go: User type + PostgresStore with Create / GetByEmail /\n  GetByID / Authenticate. Email normalized to lowercase on write and\n  read. Sentinel errors (ErrNotFound / ErrEmailTaken / ErrInvalidEmail\n  / ErrWeakPassword) for HTTP mapping without leaking pgx.\n- 17 tests total (6 password unit + 9 integration + a round-trip\n  with older params proving PHC encoding works).\n\nclients:\n- store.go: OAuth client registry. Confidential clients have a\n  hashed secret (same argon2id primitive as user passwords — why\n  roll two hashes); public clients have no secret and rely on PKCE.\n  Authenticate enforces: confidential must present secret, public\n  must not. Rejects public-with-secret as misconfig rather than\n  silently ignoring.\n- Pure policy helpers on Client: CheckRedirectURI (exact match,\n  per RFC 6749 §3.1.2.2), CheckGrant, CheckScopes (subset check).\n- 11 tests: 8 DB integration + 3 policy-helper unit.\n\nDeps added: golang.org/x/crypto/argon2, github.com/jackc/pgx/v5,\ngithub.com/google/uuid.","tree":{"sha":"063ece1ab31b289fcdb7e850ee859c16db57ebd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/063ece1ab31b289fcdb7e850ee859c16db57ebd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKDUxMDk1MzA2NDMxMGZhODg0OTI1ZDJlODViNTM0ZWEzMWY0ZjIzZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03","sha":"b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03"}],"sha":"510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/510953064310fa884925d2e85b534ea31f4f23dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-21T22:34:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-21T22:34:48Z","email":"me@matthockenbury.com","name":"Matt Hockenbury"},"message":"Initial scaffold: OIDC IdP with claims-to-tuples sync via outbox\n\nsubproject 2 of sysdesign-lab: the identity track pivot. OIDC\nauthorization server in Go with a novel twist — identity changes\n(user created, group membership added) sync to OpenFGA as FGA\ntuples via the transactional outbox pattern.\n\nDesign docs complete:\n- README §§1,3-11 (capacity + bottlenecks intentionally omitted;\n  this is a protocols/correctness project, not a scale one)\n- docs/architecture.md — component deep-dive, flow sequence diagrams\n- docs/tradeoffs.md — resolved + pending decisions\n- docs/rfcs.md — spec index + reading order, short summaries of\n  what each RFC is and where it lands in our code\n- docs/learning_objectives.md — replaces the usual \"capacity\n  estimates\" section. Explicit learning targets per matt''s gaps:\n  multi-issuer validation, downstream signature verification,\n  scope-based authz, DPoP as stretch. Each one mapped to where\n  it lives in the code + how it''s verified.\n\nStack:\n- Three binaries: idp, outbox-worker, demo-api\n- Postgres (IdP schema) + separate Postgres (OpenFGA''s store) +\n  OpenFGA v1.9.4 (Apache 2.0 ReBAC engine, pinned)\n- 8-table IdP schema: users, clients, auth codes, refresh tokens,\n  groups, memberships, consents, signing keys, sessions, fga_outbox\n\nLocked decisions:\n- JWT access tokens, no introspection\n- Refresh token rotation (Level 2, no reuse detection yet)\n- Outbox pattern for FGA sync (not sync, not CDC)\n- Basic HTML login + consent, no admin UI\n- OpenFGA storage on separate Postgres, mirrors realistic deployment\n- Postgres host port 5434 to avoid collision with url-shortener''s 5432\n- WebAuthn deferred as stretch\n\nMakefile mirrors url-shortener''s mature pattern: make up-all,\nup-app/down-app/restart-app/status-app, logs-idp/etc, with a\nhealth-gated precheck and graceful SIGTERM via nohup + PID files.\n\nNo implementation yet — package skeletons with doc.go files only.\nEmpty module builds cleanly; compose config validates.","tree":{"sha":"e7133c56aea7542ed87b7bfe2819cff42e0f5df8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/trees/e7133c56aea7542ed87b7bfe2819cff42e0f5df8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/git/commits/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2676257?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury","id":2676257,"login":"mhockenbury","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzYyNTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhockenbury","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commit/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03","node_id":"C_kwDOSJFenNoAKGIwYmRlODMyNzA5YmUzMWMzZmMyODQyNjEwYmExMGY0MTFmYzhhMDM","parents":[],"sha":"b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits/b0bde832709be31c3fc2842610ba10f411fc8a03"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/mhockenbury/identity-provider/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=1884b0ff3bb416cedde002bc6347ecde3c0f7fa1&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A21%3A57.897Z"}');
